25,"pass":true}],"assumptions":["Single pass conversion 98% and selectivity 91% are typical design values for the high conversion silver process, not fitted.","Reactor is adiabatic; the split between dehydrogenation and oxidation is solved from the heat balance at the bed outlet temperature. Hydrogen burnt in the bed is counted inside the oxidation route.","Formic acid and methyl formate (tens to hundreds of ppm) are not modelled; no ion exchange step is shown.","Methanol and water are evaporated into the air at about 70 C using heat from the first absorber stage circulation (as in the BASF type process); steam only superheats the feed.","Absorber tail gas is saturated with water; its methanol and HCHO slip is taken as zero.","Product priced on contained HCHO (formalin quotes converted at 37 wt%)."],"notes":[]}